On Wednesday 11 August 2004 14:36, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> What does "branching" mean in this case?  IMO, it's a hierarchical
> relationship in nature.  Perhaps something with both jimca and vipsu, or
> with jicmu or, for that matter, farvi?  Yeah, maybe farvi is best.

"Branching" means that one species becomes several species. {farvi} means that 
one species becomes another species. In languages, Latin branched into 
Sardinian, Romanian, Italian, Spanish, French, etc., while Attic developed 
into Modern Greek but did not branch (Tsakonian is descended from another 
ancient dialect).

